      "message": "You shouldn\u0027t need to guess if linux_musl_arm64 exists here.  It looks like you are building a single CmakeSnapshot module and expecting it to find both linux_glibc_x86_64 and linux_musl_arm64 artifacts.  It would be better to use the linux_glibc_x86_64 variant of your module to gather the linux_glibc_x86_64 variants, and the linux_musl_arm64 variant to gather the linux_musl_arm64 variants.  That would mean dropping `variations` completely and passing `nil` to `AddVariationDependencies`, which will reuse the current module\u0027s variations, and using `ctx.Os() \u003d\u003d android.LinuxMusl` to check if the current module is building for musl.",
